<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23628" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-offĭcĭōsus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>undutiful</i>, <i>inofficious.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Not observant of his duty</i>, <i>undutiful</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">humana gens inofficiosa dei,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Apol. 40</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">libertus inofficiosus patrono,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					37, 14, 1</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Contrary to one</i>'<i>s duty</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">testamentum, i. e. one in which nothing is left
					to one's nearest relatives, children, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Verr. 1, 42, 107</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Dig. 5, 2</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In partic., <i>not
				obliging</i>, <i>disobliging</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in aliquem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 13, 27, 1</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
